{
  "title": "Delete the startup photo dimension backfill",
  "description": "photos::spawn_dimension_backfill (server/src/photos/backfill.rs, started from main.rs) decodes photos that have neither width nor file_size. \
It was added in #387 for photos stored before those columns existed, and that work is done: the #387 migration filled file_size for existing photos, every photo writer (upload, scrape fetch_images, generate_photo) sets file_size, the Postgres import copied it, and a copy of the prod database on 2026-10-14 had 0 matching photos. \
All it does now is run a COUNT(*) over photos on every start. \
Delete the module and the call in main.rs. \
Keep the width/height/file_size columns and the photo_dim:/photo_size: filters. \
See doc/server-startup.md, step 5.",
